# L §4.6 step 1: "a range a..b matches every key from a to b in index order"; step 4 refuses only two candidates still
# tied, and no read has both rows as candidates when their keys don't meet (§5.3: "rows at different stated keys are
# ordered by precedence").  [1987] and [1988..1990] meet at no key; nor do [0..20] and [21] on an integer index,
# [*, k1] and [*, k2..k4], or [a, 1..3] and [a, 5].  Each read takes the one row that matches it.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
index yrs = year 1986..1990
index ages = int 0..30
index ps = [a, b]
index ks = [k1, k2, k3, k4, k5]
input top[y in yrs]: num
input rate[x in ages]: num
input cell[p in ps, k in ks]: num
input deep[p in ps, x in ages]: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  top[1987] = 0.385 "a"
  top[1988..1990] = 0.28 "b"
  rate[0..20] = 1
  rate[21] = 2
  cell[*, k1] = 3
  cell[*, k2..k4] = 4
  deep[a, 1..3] = 5
  deep[a, 5] = 6

ask q: top[1987], top[1989], rate[20], rate[21], cell[b, k1], cell[b, k3], deep[a, 2], deep[a, 5]
=== expect
q: (0.385, 0.28, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)
  cut 2026-12-31
